  骨肉团圆 | gǔ ròu tuán yuán | reunion of flesh-and-blood family members
  天伦之乐 | tiān lún zhī lè | domestic bliss; joy of family reunion
  破镜重圆 | pò jìng chóng yuán | a broken mirror made round again (reunion after separation)
  欢聚一堂 | huān jù yì táng | happily gather together under one roof

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  团 | tuán | group; round; cluster; unite | grupo; esfera; unir; reunión | 囗 | enclosure | 囗 (enclosing boundary) | 才 (talent / phonetic in simplified) | 6 | 全包围结构 | Enclosure 囗 encircling members tightly into a cohesive sphere or cluster, representing intimate solidarity. | An enclosure (囗) drawing talented loved ones (才) together into a warm circular group. | Un recinto (囗) que abraza a los seres queridos (才) en un círculo de afecto y unión. | 35 | WDI | 團
  圆 | yuán | round; circular; complete; fulfill | redondo; circular; completo | 囗 | enclosure | 囗 (round boundary) | 员 (yuán / member / round phonetic) | 10 | 全包围结构 | Enclosure 囗 wrapping around 员, depicting the round, complete shape of an ancient jade disc or the full moon, symbolizing completeness. | An enclosing circle (囗) embracing all family members (员) into harmonious wholeness like the full moon. | Un círculo exterior (囗) que envuelve a cada miembro (员) en una esfera perfecta como la luna llena. | 35 | WRBO | 圓

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Enclosing everyone in a group (团) within a complete round circle like the full moon (圆) creates a heartwarming family reunion (团圆).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Encerrar a todos en un abrazo grupal (团) dentro de un círculo pleno como la luna llena (圆) representa el reencuentro familiar (团圆).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: The circular motif in 团圆 echoes the Chinese philosophical concept of 圆满 (perfection and completeness), embodied in the full moon on Mid-Autumn night and eating round dumplings or mooncakes.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Two rising 2nd tones: tuán yuán (35-35). Both syllables rise gracefully with sustained melodic cadence.

traps_and_cognates:
