    园 | yuán | garden; park | Has 元 inside 囗 instead of 员
    圈 | quān | circle; ring | Has 卷 inside 囗 instead of 员
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    团结 | tuán jié | unite; rally together
    团体 | tuán tǐ | organization; team
    圆满 | yuán mǎn | satisfactory; complete
    原则 | yuán zé | principle; standard

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 团圆 specifically conveys the emotional, intimate joy of family members or loved ones reuniting in harmonious completeness after separation.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 团圆 vs. 聚会 | jùhuì | 团圆 carries profound emotional and cultural weight regarding family reunion and completeness, whereas 聚会 is an everyday social gathering of friends, colleagues, or clubs.
    2 | 团圆 vs. 重逢 | chóngféng | 团圆 emphasizes the warm, unified state of the whole family together, whereas 重逢 highlights the specific moment of crossing paths again after parting.
    3 | 团圆 vs. 见面 | jiànmiàn | 团圆 is a culturally solemn reunion of kin, whereas 见面 is an ordinary meeting or casual encounter between people.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 外面北风呼啸、天寒地冻，草屋内却炭火微明、饭香扑鼻。子路为父母盛上洁白的米饭。看到儿子平安归来，父母笑逐颜开，这风雪夜中的全家团圆胜过了一切荣华富贵。 | Wàimiàn běifēng hūxiào, tiānhán-dìdòng, cǎowū nèi què tànhuǒ wēimíng, fànxiāng pūbí. Zǐlù wèi fùmǔ chéng shàng jiébái de mǐfàn. Kàndào érzi píng'ān guīlái, fùmǔ xiàozhúyánkāi, zhè fēngxuě yè zhōng de quánjiā tuányuán shèngguò le yíqiè rónghuá-fùguì. | Outside, freezing winds howled, but inside the hut embers glowed and rice aroma filled the air. Zilu served bowls of pure white rice to his parents. Seeing their son return safe brought joyful smiles; this blizzard family reunion surpassed all worldly riches. | Afuera aullaba el viento gélido, pero en la choza brillaban las brasas y flotaba el dulce aroma del arroz. Zilu sirvió el blanco manjar a sus padres. Ver a su hijo regresar sano colmó sus rostros de gozo; este reencuentro familiar en la nieve superó toda la riqueza terrenal.
  #2 | 在当代跨国劳动力流动与快速城市化背景下，如何保障数以千万计在异乡打拼的建设者拥有阖家团圆的权利，成为了社会政策考量的重要议题。便捷的高铁网络和逐渐延长的带薪年假制度，正让曾经奢侈漫长的归乡团圆之旅变得更加触手可及。 | Zài dāngdài kuàguó láodònglì liúdòng yǔ kuàisù chéngshìhuà bèijǐng xià, rúhé bǎozhàng shù yǐ qiānwàn jì zài yìxiāng dǎpīn de jiànshèzhě yǒngyǒu héjiā tuányuán de quánlì, chéngwéile shèhuì zhèngcè kǎoliáng de zhòngyào yìtí. Biànjié de gāotiě wǎngluò yǔ zhújiàn yáncháng de dàixīn niánjià zhìdù, zhèng ràng céngjīng shēchǐ màncháng de guīxiāng tuányuán zhī lǚ biànde gèngjiā chùshǒu-kějí. | In the era of labor mobility and rapid urbanization, securing the right to family reunion for millions of migrant workers has become an important social policy issue. High-speed rail networks and extended paid leave are making the once-luxurious reunion journey increasingly accessible. | En el contexto de la migración laboral y la urbanización acelerada, garantizar el derecho a la reunión familiar a millones de trabajadores es un reto clave de política social. Las redes de trenes de alta velocidad y las vacaciones remuneradas hacen que el ansiado regreso al hogar sea hoy más accesible.
